sei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Photographie","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Fotograf\u00eda","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Fotografie","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/fr","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"},"pt":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/fr","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"},"en":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":"Analog Photography. As a true amateur photographer, Beckhoff\u2019s images are defined by a tangible connection between the photographer and his subjects. His approach reveals a way of taking photographs that allows a closer, more personal connection with the subject\u2014something that feels increasingly rare and, for various reasons, less possible today.","longdescr":" Raw emotions of the 1960s and \u201870s. At seventy-seven, Beckhoff, a self-taught photographer, has created a striking body of work filled with unfiltered, familiar emotion. After graduating from Philadelphia College of Textiles and Science in 1968, Beckhoff\u2019s interest in people led him to learn photography on the streets of Philadelphia. These portraits document the raw emotions of the pivotal and tumultuous 1960s and 1970s.\nAs a true amateur photographer, Beckhoff\u2019s images are defined by a tangible connection between the photographer and his subjects. His preference for black-and-white photography, rooted in tradition, highlights the interplay of light and shadow, adding a striking sense of intimacy and meaning to his work. His approach reveals a way of taking photographs that allows a closer, more personal connection with the subject\u2014something that feels increasingly rare and, for various reasons, less possible today.\nHis spontaneous images have been showcased at the Nexus Gallery in New York, and he has been invited by Nikon to exhibit in Tokyo, Japan, as well as galleries in San Miguel de Allende, Mexico. More recently, Les Rencontres d\u2019Arles in France invited him to feature in their annual photography festival.\nIn January 2025, Beckhoff's images were analog reprinted on expired films and Baryta paper at the TinyGallery in Brussels. These prints were created using a Leitz enlarger from the 1960s, adding a timeless quality and a deep connection to the era they depict.\n","performers":"Louis Robinson von Beckhoff (VS)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"},"it":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/fr","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"},"cn":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/fr","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"},"fr":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":"Photographie analogique. En tant que v\u00e9ritable photographe amateur, les images de Beckhoff se caract\u00e9risent par une connexion tangible entre le photographe et ses sujets. Son approche r\u00e9v\u00e8le une mani\u00e8re de prendre des photographies qui permet une connexion plus proche et personnelle avec le sujet \u2013 quelque chose qui semble de plus en plus rare et de moins en moins possible aujourd'hui.","longdescr":"\u00c9motions brutes des ann\u00e9es 1960 et 1970. \u00c0 septante-sept ans, Beckhoff, un photographe autodidacte, a cr\u00e9\u00e9 un corpus d'\u0153uvres saisissantes, remplies d'\u00e9motions brutes et famili\u00e8res. Apr\u00e8s avoir obtenu son dipl\u00f4me du Philadelphia College of Textiles and Science en 1968, l'int\u00e9r\u00eat de Beckhoff pour les gens l'a pouss\u00e9 \u00e0 apprendre la photographie dans les rues de Philadelphie. Ces portraits documentent les \u00e9motions brutes des ann\u00e9es 1960 et 1970, une \u00e9poque charni\u00e8re et tumultueuse.\nEn tant que v\u00e9ritable photographe amateur, les images de Beckhoff se caract\u00e9risent par une connexion tangible entre le photographe et ses sujets. Sa pr\u00e9f\u00e9rence pour la photographie en noir et blanc, ancr\u00e9e dans la tradition, met en valeur le jeu de lumi\u00e8re et d'ombre, ajoutant une forte intimit\u00e9 et une signification profonde \u00e0 son travail. Son approche r\u00e9v\u00e8le une mani\u00e8re de prendre des photos qui permet une connexion plus proche et plus personnelle avec le sujet \u2013 quelque chose qui semble de plus en plus rare et, pour diverses raisons, de moins en moins possible aujourd'hui.\nSes images spontan\u00e9es ont \u00e9t\u00e9 expos\u00e9es \u00e0 la Nexus Gallery de New York, et Nikon l'a invit\u00e9 \u00e0 exposer \u00e0 Tokyo, au Japon, ainsi que dans des galeries \u00e0 San Miguel de Allende, au Mexique. Plus r\u00e9cemment, Les Rencontres d'Arles en France l'ont invit\u00e9 \u00e0 participer \u00e0 leur festival annuel de photographie.\nEn janvier 2025, les images de Beckhoff ont \u00e9t\u00e9 r\u00e9imprim\u00e9es en analogique sur des films p\u00e9rim\u00e9s et du papier baryt\u00e9 \u00e0 la TinyGallery de Bruxelles. Ces tirages ont \u00e9t\u00e9 r\u00e9alis\u00e9s \u00e0 l'aide d'un agrandisseur Leitz des ann\u00e9es 1960, conf\u00e9rant \u00e0 ces \u0153uvres une qualit\u00e9 intemporelle et une connexion profonde avec l'\u00e9poque qu'elles d\u00e9peignent.\n","performers":"Louis Robinson von Beckhoff (USA)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/fr","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"},"sp":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/fr","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"},"nl":{"name":"Moments In Time Past","shortdescr":"\nAnaloge fotografie. Als echte amateurfotograaf worden Beckhoffs beelden gekarakteriseerd door een tastbare verbinding tussen de fotograaf en zijn onderwerpen. Zijn benadering onthult een manier van fotograferen die een hechtere, meer persoonlijke band met het onderwerp mogelijk maakt \u2013 iets dat steeds zeldzamer wordt en om verschillende redenen vandaag de dag steeds minder mogelijk lijkt.","longdescr":"Pure emoties van de jaren 1960 en 1970 Op zevenenzestigjarige leeftijd heeft Beckhoff, een autodidactische fotograaf, een indrukwekkend oeuvre gecre\u00eberd, doordrenkt van ongeremde, herkenbare emoties. Na zijn afstuderen aan het Philadelphia College of Textiles and Science in 1968, leidde Beckhoffs interesse in mensen hem ertoe om fotografie te leren op de straten van Philadelphia. Deze portretten documenteren de pure emoties van de beslissende en turbulente jaren 1960 en 1970.\n\nAls echte amateurfotograaf worden Beckhoffs beelden gekarakteriseerd door een tastbare verbinding tussen de fotograaf en zijn onderwerpen. Zijn voorkeur voor zwart-wit fotografie, geworteld in traditie, benadrukt het spel van licht en schaduw, waardoor een opvallend gevoel van intimiteit en betekenis in zijn werk ontstaat. Zijn benadering onthult een manier van fotograferen die een hechtere, persoonlijkere band met het onderwerp mogelijk maakt \u2013 iets dat steeds zeldzamer en om verschillende redenen vandaag de dag minder goed mogelijk lijkt.\n\nZijn spontane beelden zijn getoond in de Nexus Gallery in New York, en Nikon nodigde hem uit om in Tokio, Japan, te exposeren, evenals in galeries in San Miguel de Allende, Mexico. Meer recentelijk werd hij uitgenodigd door Les Rencontres d\u2019Arles in Frankrijk om deel te nemen aan hun jaarlijkse fotografie-festival.\n\nIn januari 2025 werden Beckhoffs beelden analoog opnieuw afgedrukt op vervallen films en barytpapier in de TinyGallery in Brussel. Deze afdrukken werden gemaakt met een Leitz vergrootapparaat uit de jaren 1960, waardoor ze een tijdloze kwaliteit en een diepe verbinding met het tijdperk dat ze afbeelden, krijgen.","performers":"Louis Robinson von Beckhoff (VS)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/tinygallery.photo\/nl","email":"olivier@tinygallery.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 475 27 95 56","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005365"}},"place":{"id":275243,"translations":{"de":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"TinyGallery - Small museum of amateur photography - wishes to preserve amateur photography and pay tribute to the anonymous artists who authored them.\r\n\r\nWhether produced intentionally or accidentally, amateur photography fascinates us with its spontaneous creations. Magical, raw moments are captured, allowing us an intimate insight into the lives of strangers who lived over a century ago. In a nod to the vanity of the ephemeral, these benevolent ghosts, who have long been protected by the shadows of the past, surprise us with their proximity. Battered and bruised albums scattered over flea markets surrender to us defencelessly, bearing witness to a time when photography was not considered dangerous. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"La TinyGallery - Petit mus\u00e9e de la photographie amateur - veut conserver la photographie amateur et rendre hommage \u00e0 leurs auteurs, ces artistes anonymes.\r\n\r\nIntentionnelle ou accidentelle, la photographie amateur nous fascine par ses cr\u00e9ations spontan\u00e9es. Instants magiques et bruts o\u00f9 nous entrons dans l\u2019intimit\u00e9 de ces inconnus \u00e0 plus d\u2019un si\u00e8cle de distance. Clins d'oeil \u00e0 la vanit\u00e9 de l'\u00e9ph\u00e9m\u00e8re, ces fant\u00f4mes bienveillants longtemps prot\u00e9g\u00e9s dans l\u2019ombre des albums nous surprennent par leur proximit\u00e9. Albums d\u00e9piaut\u00e9s, dispers\u00e9s, brocant\u00e9s, se livrant et sans d\u00e9fenses, ils sont les t\u00e9moins d\u2019un temps o\u00f9 la photographie n'\u00e9tait pas consid\u00e9r\u00e9e comme dangereuse. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Rue de la Cuve","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Cuve, 26","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"TinyGallery Brussels","address_street_name":"Kuipstraat","address_street_number":"26","address_street_box":null,"email":"ogc@ogc.be","website":"http:\/\/www.tinygallery.photo","phone_contact":"+32 475 27 95 56","phone_booking":"+32 472 27 95 56","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Elsene","address_line1":"Kuipstraat, 26","address_line2":"1050 Elsene","description_web":"TinyGallery - Klein museum voor amateurfotografie - wil de amateurfotografie conserveren en hulde brengen aan hun auteurs, deze anonieme kunstenaars.\r\n\r\nAmateurfotografie fascineert ons door de spontane creaties. Ze ontstaan doelbewust of ongewild, die magische en authentieke fragmenten van de intimiteit van onbekenden die meer dan een eeuw geleden leefden. Een knipoog naar de ijdelheid van het kortstondige, welwillende geesten die lang beschermd waren in de schaduw van vergeten albums. Ze verrassen ons met hun nabijheid, intieme albums die weerloos opengerukt eindigden op de rommelmarkt, stille getuigen van een tijd waarin fotografie niet als gevaarlijk werd beschouwd. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[5],"translations":{"de":["Flagey"],"pt":[null],"en":["Flagey"],"it":["Flagey"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Flagey"],"sp":["Flagey"],"nl":["Flagey"]}},"zones":{"list":[21],"translations":{"de":["S\u00fcden"],"pt":[null],"en":["Sout