runfaut. Conceived as a symbolist and dreamlike universe, the house is one of the masterpieces of art nouveau in Brussels, a union of Belgian and French art of the time. \r\nJules Brunfaut, unfamiliar with the new style, was inspired by other architects' houses, such as those of Victor Horta (personal house, Tassel and Wessinger hotels), Ernest Bl\u00e9rot (personal house, now destroyed) and Octave Van Rysselbeghe and Henry Van de Velde (Otlet hotel). \r\nCombining the beaux-arts style with that of modernity, or art nouveau at that period, the Maison Hannon is a singular work, an intimate and personal house, bringing together the tastes and passions of its commissioners. \r\n\r\nThe Maison Hannon will open its doors to the public on June 1, 2023, as a house museum. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/www.ticketing.brussels\/en\/tickets\/event-details.Maison-Hannon.536bea1a-2f73-4284-9db1-dd3b861df83b","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Maison Hannon","address_street_name":"Avenue de la Jonction","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@maisonhannon.be","website":"https:\/\/maisonhannon.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1060","address_city":"Saint-Gilles","address_line1":"Avenue de la Jonction, 1","address_line2":"1060 Saint-Gilles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Maison Hannon","address_street_name":"Avenue de la Jonction","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@maisonhannon.be","website":"https:\/\/maisonhannon.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1060","address_city":"Saint-Gilles","address_line1":"Avenue de la Jonction, 1","address_line2":"1060 Saint-Gilles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Maison Han