a by Carlos Ruiz Vale as part of The Photo Brussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005358"},"en":{"name":"Psyche Flora by Carlos Ruiz Vale as part of The Photo Brussels Festival","shortdescr":"\nBlending technical precision with a painterly sensibility, Ruiz Valle\u2019s work resonates with an emotive power that transcends the visual medium. Flora Psyche offers an intimate glimpse into the artist\u2019s world, celebrating the enduring connections between nature, identity, and self-expression. \n","longdescr":"THE ARTIST \/\/ CARLOS RUIZ VALLE \nCarlos Ruiz Valle (b. 1989, Campana, Argentina) has been passionate about art from an early age. Inspired by anime, he was later drawn to photography. As a teenager in Buenos Aires, he began documenting the city with his first mobile phone, a Nokia 5230, capturing its streets, people, and architecture. At 17, Ruiz joined a parkour group. As their popularity grew, Ruiz purchased a Canon 60D to document their performances. During this period, Ruiz began to recognise his distinct photographic vision.  \nAt 23, Ruiz moved to M\u00e1laga to study photography at San Telmo Art School. He further broadened his artistic influences by visiting exhibitions in Madrid, Paris, Arles, and Amsterdam. The 2020 COVID-19 pandemic proved a turning point for Ruiz, sparking a personal project that led to self-exploration and the development of his distinctive photographic style.  \nThe work of Ruiz is inspired by artists such as Jackson Pollock, Rembrandt, Herb Ritts, and Helmut Newton. Characterised by a medium-short portrait style, his photographs often incorporate his body and flowers. He captures raw, emotional moments using a Canon 80D. His art evolves with each project, revealing new layers of emotional depth. \n","performers":"The Palm Beach Gallery is honoured to host Flora Psyche, the first solo exhibition by Malaga-based photographer Carlos Ruiz Valle. Presented as part of the ninth edition of the Photo Brussels Festival, this exhibition marks a milestone in the artist\u2019s career. It showcases three evocative series that explore themes of identity, self-discovery, and gender fluidity. ","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005358"},"it":{"name":"Psyche Flora by Carlos Ruiz Vale as part of The Photo Brussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005358"},"cn":{"name":"Psyche Flora by Carlos Ruiz Vale as part of The Photo Brussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005358"},"fr":{"name":"Psyche Flora by Carlos Ruiz Vale as part of The Photo Brussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005358"},"sp":{"name":"Psyche Flora by Carlos Ruiz Vale as part of The Photo Brussels Festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"