soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2025-01-28T08:52:11+01:00","published_at":"2025-01-28T08:46:51+01:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":316994,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"concert","ranking":1.2599210498948732,"languages":{"spoken":["fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":1,"translations":{"de":"Konzert","pt":null,"en":"Concert","it":"Concerti","cn":null,"fr":"Concert","sp":"Concierto","nl":"Concert"}},"others":{"list":[2],"translations":{"de":["Klassisch"],"pt":[null],"en":["Classical"],"it":["Classica"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Classique"],"sp":["Cl\u00e1sica"],"nl":["Klassiek"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, violin - works by Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"},"pt":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, violin - works by Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"},"en":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, violin - works by Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":"Programme :\n\nBACH Sonata No 3 for violin and harpsichord in E M, BWV 1016\nBEETHOVEN Sonata No 9 for violin and piano in C m, Op 47 \u2018\u00e0 Kreutzer \nDEBUSSY Sonata for violin and piano, (CD 148)\n ","longdescr":"SIMON VASKOU, piano :\n\nBorn in Grenoble, France, in 1994, Simon Vaskou began playing the piano at the age of 4 and entered Grenoble's Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) at the age of 6. He continued his musical studies at the Conservatoire until joining the C.E.P.I. (cycle d'enseignement \u00e0 destination pr\u00e9-professionnel) in 2010.\n\nIn 2013, he left Grenoble to specialise in Paris and was admitted to the Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) de Paris. In 2015, he obtained his D.E.M. (Dipl\u00f4me d'\u00c9tudes Musicales) from the C.R.R. in Paris, as well as a Licence in Musicology from the Universit\u00e9 Paris-Sorbonne. He then spent two years perfecting his skills with David Braslawsky and Romano Pallottini at the Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) de Saint-Maur (Paris region), before joining the ARTS\u00b2 - Conservatoire Royal Sup\u00e9rieur school based in Mons (Belgium), in J-M Dayez's class in 2017, in the 3rd year of the Bachelor of Arts in Piano, where he passed his Bachelor of Arts with distinction.\n\nFollowing this, in September 2018, he joined the Koninklijk Conservatorium Brussel (K.C.B.)for a Master degree in the class of Jan Michiels. In June 2020, he obtained his Master of Arts degree with distinction, performing S. Rachmaninov's Concerto No. 3, Op. 30.\n\nHe has also taken part in master-classes, taken lessons and met many renowned pianists and teachers, including Denis Pascal, Florent Boffard, Georges Pludermacher, Alexandre Tharaud, Kotaro Fukuma and Jean-Philippe Collard. He has been lucky enough to perform in venues such as the M.C.2 (Grenoble, FR), the Salle Stekel (Grenoble, FR), the Salle Colonne (Paris, FR), the T-Hotel (Cagliari, IT), the Concertzaal at the Koninklijk Conservatorium (Brussels, BE), the Atelier Marcel Hastir (Brussels, BE), the Tricoterie (Brussels, BE), the Salle Franz Liszt at the Conservatoire (Geneva, CH), and the Konzersaal at the Universit\u00e4t der K\u00fcnste (Berlin, DE).\n\nHe has also taken part in numerous summer academies, such as the Acad\u00e9mies Internationales d'\u00c9t\u00e9 du Grand Nancy (FR), the Acad\u00e9mies de Flaine (FR), Music'Alp (FR) and Pireneos Classics (ES); he is also a prizewinner in the Online Sviatoslav Richter International Piano Competition 2024 (2nd prize).\n\nAt the same time, he also pursued a career as a teacher, obtaining his Master's degree in Music Pedagogy with distinction from the Conservatoire Royal de Bruxelles (C.R.B.) in 2023. Since then, he has taught at several academies in the Brussels-Capital region, including the Acad\u00e9mie de Woluwe-Saint-Lambert and the Acad\u00e9mie de Jette.\n\nJULIEN OLIVE, violin :\n\nBorn in France, he began violin at the CRR in Bordeaux. After obtaining his DEM, he left in 2015 to study at the Koninklijk Conservatorium Brussel in Naaman Sluchin's class. He obtained his master's degree there in 2020.\n\nDuring his studies, he was fortunate enough to receive advice from Miriam Fried, Marina Chiche, Joanna Matkowska, the Voce Quartet, Tony Nys, Anne Estelle M\u00e9douze and Claire D\u00e9sert, among others.\n \nHe has also played in a number of orchestras, including the Netherlands Youth Orchestra, the Animato Foundation Chamber Orchestra, the Hector Berlioz Young European Orchestra, the Maastricht Academy Chamber Orchestra and, more recently, the Op\u00e9ra de Rouen Normandie, the Brussels Philharmonic and the Belgian National Orchestra, under conductors including Fran\u00e7ois Xavier Roth, Kazushi Ono, Sir Roger Norrington, Kevin Griffith, Holly Hyun Choe and Ben Glassberg.\nThese various projects have taken him to Italy, Amsterdam, Rotterdam, Berlin, Vienna, Bucharest, Prague and Paris.\n","performers":"Simon Vaskou (piano); Julien Olive (violin)\n ","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"},"it":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, violin - works by Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"},"cn":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, violin - works by Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"},"fr":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, violon \u2013 oeuvres de Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":"Programme :\n\nBACH Sonate n\u00b03 pour violon et clavecin en mi M, BWV 1016\nBEETHOVEN Sonate n\u00b09 pour violon et piano en do m, op 47 \u00ab \u00e0 Kreutzer \u00bb \nDEBUSSY Sonate pou violon et piano, (CD 148)","longdescr":"SIMON VASKOU, piano :\n\nN\u00e9 \u00e0 Grenoble en France en 1994, Simon Vaskou d\u00e9bute le piano \u00e0 l\u2019\u00e2ge de 4 ans et entre au Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) de Grenoble \u00e0 6 ans. Il poursuit ses \u00e9tudes musicales dans cet \u00e9tablissement, jusqu\u2019\u00e0 y int\u00e9grer le C.E.P.I.(cycle d\u2019enseignement \u00e0 destination pr\u00e9-professionnel), en 2010.\n\nEn 2013, il quitte Grenoble pour se sp\u00e9cialiser \u00e0 Paris et est admis en cycle sp\u00e9cialis\u00e9 au Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R) de Paris. Parall\u00e8lement, il poursuit des \u00e9tudes de musicologie \u00e0 l\u2019universit\u00e9 Paris-Sorbonne.En 2015, il obtient son D.E.M. (Dipl\u00f4me d\u2019\u00c9tudes Musicales) au C.R.R. de Paris, ainsi qu\u2019une Licence en Musicologie de l\u2019Universit\u00e9 Paris-Sorbonne. Il se perfectionne ensuite deux ans avec David Braslawsky et Romano Pallottini au Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) de Saint-Maur (R\u00e9gion Parisienne), avant d\u2019int\u00e9grer l\u2019\u00e9cole ARTS\u00b2 \u2013 Conservatoire Royal Sup\u00e9rieur bas\u00e9e \u00e0 Mons (Belgique), dans la classe de J-M Dayez en 2017, en 3e ann\u00e9e de Bachelor pianistique. ll y r\u00e9ussit brillamment son \u201cBachelor of Arts\u201d avec distinction.\n\n\u00c0 la suite de cela, en septembre 2018, il int\u00e8gre le Koninklijk Conservatorium Brussel (K.C.B.) en Master dans la classe de Jan Michiels. En juin 2020, il obtient son dipl\u00f4me de \u00ab Master of Arts \u00bb avec distinction, interpr\u00e9tant le concerto n\u00b03 de S.Rachmaninov op.30.\n\nIl a aussi particip\u00e9 \u00e0 des \u00ab master-class \u00bb, pris des cours, et rencontr\u00e9 de nombreux pianistes et professeurs r\u00e9put\u00e9s, comme Denis Pascal, Florent Boffard, Georges Pludermacher, Alexandre Tharaud, Kotaro Fukuma ou encore Jean-Philippe Collard. Il a eu la chance de se produire dans diff\u00e9rentes salles tels que la M.C.2 (Grenoble, FR), la Salle Stekel (Grenoble, FR) la Salle Colonne (Paris, FR), le T-Hotel (Cagliari, IT), la Concertzaal du Koninklijk Conservatorium (Bruxelles, BE), l\u2019\u00ab Atelier Marcel Hastir \u00bb (Bruxelles, BE), \u00ab la Tricoterie \u00bb (Bruxelles, BE), la salle Franz Liszt du Conservatoire (Gen\u00e8ve, CH), ou la Konzersaal de l\u2019Universit\u00e4t der K\u00fcnste (Berlin, DE).\n\nIl a \u00e9galement particip\u00e9 \u00e0 de nombreuses Acad\u00e9mies d\u2019\u00e9t\u00e9 tels que \u00ab Acad\u00e9mies Internationales d\u2019\u00c9t\u00e9 du Grand Nancy \u00bb (FR), \u00ab Acad\u00e9mies de Flaine \u00bb (FR), \u00ab Music\u2019Alp \u00bb (FR) ou \u00ab Pireneos Classics \u00bb (ES);  il est \u00e9galement laur\u00e9at de Concours International: Online \u00ab Sviatoslav Richter \u00bb International Piano Competition 2024 (2e prix).\n\nEn parall\u00e8le, il poursuit \u00e9galement une carri\u00e8re de p\u00e9dagogue, et obtient son Master de P\u00e9dagogie musicale avec mention au Conservatoire Royal de Bruxelles (C.R.B.) en 2023. Depuis, il enseigne dans plusieurs Acad\u00e9mies de la r\u00e9gion de Bruxelles-Capitale, tels que l\u2019Acad\u00e9mie de Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, ou de Jette.\n\n \n\n\n\nJULIEN OLIVE, violon :\n\nN\u00e9 en France, il commence le violon au CRR de Bordeaux. Apr\u00e8s son DEM obtenu il part \u00e9tudier \u00e0 partir de 2015 au Koninklijk Conservatorium Brussel dans la classe de Naaman Sluchin. Il y obtient son master en 2020.\n\nAu cours de ses \u00e9tudes, il a eu la chance de recevoir les conseils notamment de Miriam Fried, Marina Chiche, Joanna Matkowska, le quatuor Voce, Tony Nys, Anne Estelle M\u00e9douze et Claire D\u00e9sert.\n \nParall\u00e8lement il joue dans plusieurs formations d\u2019orchestre comme l\u2019orchestre des jeunes des Pays-Bas, l\u2019orchestre de chambre de la fondation Animato, le jeune orchestre europ\u00e9en Hector Berlioz, le Maastricht Academy Chamber Orchestra et plus r\u00e9cemment l\u2019op\u00e9ra de Rouen Normandie, le Brussels Philharmonic et le Belgian National Orchestra sous la direction de chefs tel que Fran\u00e7ois Xavier Roth, Kazushi Ono, sir Roger Norrington, Kevin Griffith, Holly Hyun Choe, Ben Glassberg.\nCes diff\u00e9rents projets l\u2019ont amen\u00e9 \u00e0 jouer en Italie, Amsterdam, Rotterdam, Berlin, Vienne, Bucarest, Prague ainsi que Paris.\n ","performers":"Simon Vaskou (piano); Julien Olive (violon)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"},"sp":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, violin - works by Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"},"nl":{"name":"Simon Vaskou, piano & Julien Olive, viool - werken van Bach, Beethoven, Debussy","shortdescr":"Programma :\n\nBACH -  Sonate nr. 3 voor viool en klavecimbel in E M, BWV 1016\nBEETHOVEN -  Sonate nr. 9 voor viool en piano in C m, Op 47 \u201c\u00e0 Kreutzer \nDEBUSSY -  Sonate voor viool en piano, (CD 148)\n \n\n ","longdescr":"SIMON VASKOU, piano :\n\nSimon Vaskou, geboren in Grenoble (Frankrijk) in 1994, begon op 4-jarige leeftijd piano te spelen en ging op 6-jarige leeftijd naar het Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) in Grenoble. Hij zette zijn muzikale studies voort aan hetzelfde instituut en sloot zich in 2010 aan bij het C.E.P.I. (cycle d'enseignement \u00e0 destination pr\u00e9-professionnel).\n\nIn 2013 verliet hij Grenoble om zich te specialiseren in Parijs en werd hij toegelaten tot het Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) de Paris. In 2015 behaalde hij zijn D.E.M. (Dipl\u00f4me d'\u00c9tudes Musicales) aan het C.R.R. in Parijs, evenals een licentiaat in de muziekwetenschappen aan de Universit\u00e9 Paris-Sorbonne. Vervolgens perfectioneerde hij zijn vaardigheden twee jaar lang bij David Braslawsky en Romano Pallottini aan het Conservatoire \u00e0 Rayonnement R\u00e9gional (C.R.R.) de Saint-Maur (regio Parijs), voordat hij zich in 2017 aansloot bij de ARTS\u00b2 - Koninklijke Sup\u00e9rieur Conservatorium in Bergen (Belgi\u00eb), in de klas van J-M Dayez, in het 3e jaar van de Bachelor of Arts in pianostudies, waar hij met glans slaagde voor zijn Bachelor of Arts met onderscheiding.\n\nDaarna, in september 2018, vervoegde hij het Koninklijk Conservatorium Brussel (K.C.B.) voor een Master in de klas van Jan Michiels. In juni 2020 behaalde hij zijn Master of Arts diploma met onderscheiding, waarbij hij het Concerto No. 3, Op. 30 van S. Rachmaninov vertolkte.\n\nHij nam ook deel aan masterclasses, volgde lessen en ontmoette vele gerenommeerde pianisten en docenten, waaronder Denis Pascal, Florent Boffard, Georges Pludermacher, Alexandre Tharaud, Kotaro Fukuma en Jean-Philippe Collard. Hij heeft het geluk gehad om op te treden in zalen als het M.C.2 (Grenoble, FR), de Salle Stekel (Grenoble, FR), de Salle Colonne (Parijs, FR), het T-Hotel (Cagliari, IT), de Concertzaal van het Koninklijk Conservatorium (Brussel, BE), het Atelier Marcel Hastir (Brussel, BE), de Tricoterie (Brussel, BE), de Salle Franz Liszt van het Conservatorium (Gen\u00e8ve, CH) en de Konzertsaal van de Universit\u00e4t der K\u00fcnste (Berlijn, DE).\n\nHij heeft ook deelgenomen aan talrijke zomeracademies, zoals de Acad\u00e9mies Internationales d'\u00c9t\u00e9 du Grand Nancy (FR), de Acad\u00e9mies de Flaine (FR), Music'Alp (FR) en Pireneos Classics (ES); hij is ook prijswinnaar van het Online Sviatoslav Richter International Piano Competition 2024 (2e prijs).\n\nTegelijkertijd zette hij ook zijn carri\u00e8re als docent voort en behaalde hij een Master in Muziekpedagogie met onderscheiding aan het Koninklijk Conservatorium van Brussel (C.R.B.) in 2023. Sindsdien geeft hij les aan verschillende academies in het Brussels Hoofdstedelijk Gewest, waaronder de Academie de Sint-Lambrechts-Woluwe en de Academie van Jette.","performers":"Simon Vaskou (piano); Julien Olive (viool)\n ","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-02-08-simon-vaskou-piano-julien-olive-violon\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700005878"}},"place":{"id":242272,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Atelier Marcel Hastir ist ein Ort der Kunst, der kulturellen und k\u00fcnstlerischen Begegnungen, der 1935 von dem Maler Marcel Hastir in seinem K\u00fcnstleratelier in der Rue du Commerce 51 eingerichtet wurde. Das ungew\u00f6hnliche Haus hei\u00dft seit Jahrzehnten inmitten der Kunstwerke sowohl junge K\u00fcnstler als auch gro\u00dfe Namen der belgischen und internationalen Musik- und Theaterszene willkommen - ein Ort, der mit seiner ganz besonderen Atmosph\u00e4re verzaubert.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Handelsstraat","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Handelsstraat, 51","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"The Atelier Marcel Hastir is a magical place where culture lovers and artists meet in the midst of Marcel Hastir's paintings, in the intimate setting of what has been his place of work since 1935.\r\nMarcel Hastir was a Belgian painter, theosofist and resistance fighter. His studio in the Leopold district served also as a concert hall for young musicians, and during the Second World War this \"painters school\" actually served as a relatively safe meeting place for young artists, students and resistance fighters. A team of passionate volunteers work for the preservation of his work and home organising concerts with both young and confirmed talent from Belgium and abroad.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Le nom Marcel Hastir vous dit quelque chose ?  Ce peintre, th\u00e9osophe et r\u00e9sistant belge a v\u00e9cu durant 76 ans (de 1935 jusqu\u2019\u00e0 sa mort) dans la rue du Commerce situ\u00e9e dans le quartier L\u00e9opold \u00e0 Bruxelles. Vous pouvez toujours y admirer ses toiles tout en appr\u00e9ciant de la musique classique ou du th\u00e9\u00e2tre. De grands noms du monde de la musique viennent dans ce lieu sp\u00e9cial depuis des d\u00e9cennies. L'atmosph\u00e8re intime et magique ne vous laissera pas indiff\u00e9rent.    \r\n\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Handelsstraat","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Handelsstraat, 51","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Zegt de naam Marcel Hastir je wat? Hij was een Belgisch kunstschilder, theosoof en verzetsstrijder. Van 1935 tot aan zijn dood 76 jaar later woonde hij in de Handelsstraat in de Brusselse Leopoldwijk. Je kan er zijn doeken nog steeds bewonderen terwijl je geniet van klassieke muziek of theater. Al decennialang komen op deze bijzondere plek grote namen uit de muziekwereld over de vloer. De intieme en magische sfeer zal je niet onberoerd laten.  ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"de":["Europ\u00e4isches Viertel"],"pt":[null],"en":["European Quarter"],"it":["Quartiere europeo"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"sp":["Barrio Europeo"],"nl":["Europese wijk"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"de":["Osten"],"pt":[null],"en":["East"],"it":["Est"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Est"],"sp":["Este"],"nl":["Oost"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":"AtelierMarcelHastir","backoffice_id":4704,"location":{"lat":50.8420134,"lon":4.3685574},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2024-10-24T10:12:29+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:17:42+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":242272,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Atelier Marcel Hastir ist ein Ort der Kunst, der kulturellen und k\u00fcnstlerischen Begegnungen, der 1935 von dem Maler Marcel Hastir in seinem K\u00fcnstleratelier in der Rue du Commerce 51 eingerichtet wurde. Das ungew\u00f6hnliche Haus hei\u00dft seit Jahrzehnten inmitten der Kunstwerke sowohl junge K\u00fcnstler als auch gro\u00dfe Namen der belgischen und internationalen Musik- und Theaterszene willkommen - ein Ort, der mit seiner ganz besonderen Atmosph\u00e4re verzaubert.","d